 "result": "Look in these places:\n\n- **`src/tessel/ctx.py:445` (`pop(exc=None)`)**: the app context's pop is where teardown starts. At line 496 it calls `self.app.run_app_teardowns(self, exc)`.\n- **`src/tessel/ctx.py:516` (`__exit__`)**: this calls `self.pop(exc_value)`. So a `with` block that exits cleanly passes `None`, and one that exits on an unhandled exception passes that exception.\n- **`src/tessel/app.py:1616`**: the `ctx.pop(error)` call from the request-handling path, which passes the unhandled request error, or `None` if there wasn't one.\n- **`src/tessel/app.py:1453` (`run_app_teardowns`)**: this iterates `on_app_teardown_funcs` in reverse registration order and passes `exc` to each.\n- **`tests/test_appctx.py`**: examples of both the exception and `None` cases.\n\nSo the argument is the unhandled exception raised while the context was active, or `None` if the context exited normally. An exception that was handled by an error handler arrives as `None`.",
